  "id": "segregation-analysis",
  "term": "segregation analysis",
  "definition": "Segregation analysis is a method used to examine how a trait appears across families in order to test its mode of inheritance or transmission. In this context, it was used to assess whether a color-perception trait might reflect a major genetic effect rather than a simple Mendelian pattern alone.",
